<title>POLAND: Amoco to close Polish gas unit.</title>
<headline>Amoco to close Polish gas unit.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Amoco Corp. will close down its Polish gas unit this year because it decided that methane exploration in Poland would not be profitable, newspapers reported on Saturday.</p>
<p>&quot;The decision has practically been taken. We are only waiting for our headquarters in Houston to approve it,&quot; Rzeczpospolita daily quoted president of Amoco Poland Ltd, Gary Taylor, as saying.</p>
<p>Amoco has been drilling for methane in the southern region of Silesia for three years. Last year, the company decided to close down its Polish fuels distribution unit. --Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
